public import Mathlib.Data.List.Chain
public import TauCeti.GroupTheory.Coxeter.Parabolic

/-!
# Rank-two standard parabolic subgroups, and Tits' lemma

Let `cs : CoxeterSystem M W` and let `i ≠ i'` be two indices. The standard parabolic subgroup
`cs.parabolic {i, i'}` is generated by the two involutions `s i` and `s i'`, so it is a dihedral
group, and the words that spell its elements are the **alternating words** of Mathlib's
`CoxeterSystem.alternatingWord`. This file proves that, and extracts from it **Tits' lemma**: an
element with two distinct left descents has a rank-two parabolic factor that is spelled by *both*
alternating words of its length, and that length is exactly the order of the rotation `s i * s i'`.

Three steps carry the whole file.

* A reduced word has no two adjacent equal letters (`CoxeterSystem.IsReduced.isChain_ne`), because
  deleting such a pair shortens the word without changing its product. A list in two letters with
  no adjacent repetition is an alternating word
  (`CoxeterSystem.eq_alternatingWord_of_forall_mem_pair`), so a reduced word for an element of
  `cs.parabolic {i, i'}` is one of the two alternating words of its length.
* The two alternating words of a given length have the same product exactly when the rotation
  `s i * s i'` is killed by that length
  (`CoxeterSystem.wordProd_alternatingWord_eq_comm_iff`), and the alternating words repeat with
  period twice the order of that rotation
  (`CoxeterSystem.wordProd_alternatingWord_add_two_mul`). Both are direct computations from
  `CoxeterSystem.prod_alternatingWord_eq_mul_pow`, and they are the only place the dihedral
  arithmetic enters.
* A left descent `i` of `w` turns a reduced word for `s i * w` into a reduced word for `w`
  beginning with `i`. If both `i` and `i'` are left descents of a parabolic `w`, that produces two
  reduced words for `w` with different first letters, hence — the two alternating words being the
  only candidates — *both* alternating words of length `ℓ w` spell `w`.

Together these pin the length down: an element of `cs.parabolic {i, i'}` with both `i` and `i'` as
left descents has length exactly `orderOf (s i * s i')`
(`CoxeterSystem.length_eq_orderOf_of_isLeftDescent_pair`). The first two steps give that the order
divides the length; periodicity keeps the length below twice the order, and divisibility then
forces equality.

## The remaining gap to Matsumoto's theorem

Tits' lemma is classically stated with the Coxeter-matrix entry `M i i'` in place of the order of
the rotation. The two do agree — that is Tits' theorem on the geometric representation of a
Coxeter system — but all that is available from Mathlib is the divisibility
`orderOf (s i * s i') ∣ M i i'` (`CoxeterSystem.simple_mul_simple_pow`); the geometric
representation of an abstract Coxeter system is in neither Mathlib nor this repository. So the
statements below are phrased with `orderOf (s i * s i')`, which is what this combinatorics
determines on its own, and `CoxeterSystem.length_le_of_isLeftDescent_pair` records the bound by
`M i i'` that the divisibility yields.

That exactness is the one input still separating this file from Matsumoto's theorem, and it is
deliberately not assumed here. A braid move of `TauCeti/GroupTheory/Coxeter/BraidEquivalence.lean`
rewrites an alternating word of length `M i i'`, so promoting Tits' lemma to the induction step of
Matsumoto — two braid-equivalent reduced words for `w`, one beginning with `i` and one with `i'` —
needs the parabolic factor to have length `M i i'` on the nose, which is exactly the missing
statement.

## Main results

* `CoxeterSystem.IsReduced.isChain_ne`: a reduced word has no two adjacent equal letters.
* `CoxeterSystem.eq_alternatingWord_of_forall_mem_pair` and
  `CoxeterSystem.eq_alternatingWord_or_of_forall_mem_pair`: a list in two letters with no adjacent
  repetition is an alternating word.
* `CoxeterSystem.wordProd_alternatingWord_eq_of_mem_parabolic_pair`: **every element of a rank-two
  standard parabolic subgroup is spelled by an alternating word of its own length.**
* `CoxeterSystem.wordProd_alternatingWord_eq_comm_iff`: the two alternating words of length `m`
  have the same product exactly when `(s i * s i') ^ m = 1`.
* `CoxeterSystem.wordProd_alternatingWord_add_two_mul`: the products of the alternating words
  repeat with period twice the order of `s i * s i'`.
* `CoxeterSystem.wordProd_alternatingWord_eq_of_isLeftDescent_pair`: **an element of a rank-two
  standard parabolic subgroup with two distinct left descents is spelled by both alternating words
  of its length**, hence `CoxeterSystem.pow_length_eq_one_of_isLeftDescent_pair` and
  `CoxeterSystem.length_eq_orderOf_of_isLeftDescent_pair`: **that length is the order of
  `s i * s i'`**, and so at most `M i i'`
  (`CoxeterSystem.length_le_of_isLeftDescent_pair`).
* `CoxeterSystem.exists_mem_parabolic_pair_mul_of_isLeftDescent_pair`: the rank-two parabolic
  factor of an element with two distinct left descents inherits both descents.
* `CoxeterSystem.exists_wordProd_alternatingWord_mul_of_isLeftDescent_pair`: **Tits' lemma.**

## References

* A. Björner and F. Brenti, *Combinatorics of Coxeter Groups*, Springer GTM 231 (2005),
  Sections 2.2 and 3.3.
* J. E. Humphreys, *Reflection Groups and Coxeter Groups*, CUP (1990), Sections 1.9 and 5.12.
* [Root-systems roadmap](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCetiRoadmap/blob/main/TauCetiRoadmap/RepresentationTheory/RootSystems/README.md),
  Layer 3, "Matsumoto's theorem".
-/

public section

namespace CoxeterSystem

variable {B W : Type*} [Group W] {M : CoxeterMatrix B} (cs : CoxeterSystem M W)

local prefix:100 "s " => cs.simple
local prefix:100 "π " => cs.wordProd
local prefix:100 "ℓ " => cs.length

/-! ### Words in two letters -/

/-- The inductive core of `CoxeterSystem.eq_alternatingWord_of_forall_mem_pair`, with the length
of the word made explicit so that the induction may exchange the two letters. -/
private theorem eq_alternatingWord_aux :
    ∀ (n : ℕ) (i i' : B) (ω : List B), ω.length = n → (∀ j ∈ ω, j = i ∨ j = i') →
      ω.IsChain (· ≠ ·) → (∀ j ∈ ω.getLast?, j = i') → ω = alternatingWord i i' n := by
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero =>
      intro i i' ω hlen _ _ _
      rw [List.length_eq_zero_iff] at hlen
      simp [hlen, alternatingWord]
  | succ n ih =>
      intro i i' ω hlen hmem hchain hlast
      obtain rfl | ⟨σ, a, rfl⟩ := List.eq_nil_or_concat' ω
      · simp at hlen
      have ha : i' = a := (hlast a (by simp)).symm
      subst ha
      have hσlen : σ.length = n := by simpa using hlen
      obtain ⟨hσchain, -, hjoin⟩ := List.isChain_append.mp hchain
      have hσ : σ = alternatingWord i' i n := by
        refine ih i' i σ hσlen (fun j hj => (hmem j (by simp [hj])).symm) hσchain ?_
        intro j hj
        have hjne : j ≠ i' := hjoin j hj i' (by simp)
        have hjmem : j ∈ σ := List.mem_of_mem_getLast? hj
        exact (hmem j (by simp [hjmem])).resolve_right hjne
      rw [alternatingWord_succ, hσ]
      simp

/-- **A list in two letters with no adjacent repetition is an alternating word.** If every letter
of `ω` is `i` or `i'`, no two adjacent letters are equal, and the last letter is `i'`, then `ω` is
the alternating word of its own length ending in `i'`. -/
theorem eq_alternatingWord_of_forall_mem_pair {i i' : B} {ω : List B}
    (hmem : ∀ j ∈ ω, j = i ∨ j = i') (hchain : ω.IsChain (· ≠ ·))
    (hlast : ∀ j ∈ ω.getLast?, j = i') : ω = alternatingWord i i' ω.length :=
  eq_alternatingWord_aux ω.length i i' ω rfl hmem hchain hlast

/-- **A list in two letters with no adjacent repetition is one of the two alternating words of its
length.** Which of the two it is, is decided by its last letter. -/
theorem eq_alternatingWord_or_of_forall_mem_pair {i i' : B} {ω : List B}
    (hmem : ∀ j ∈ ω, j = i ∨ j = i') (hchain : ω.IsChain (· ≠ ·)) :
    ω = alternatingWord i i' ω.length ∨ ω = alternatingWord i' i ω.length := by
  rcases hgl : ω.getLast? with - | a
  · have hnil : ω = [] := List.getLast?_eq_none_iff.mp hgl
    subst hnil
    exact Or.inl (by simp [alternatingWord])
  · have hamem : a ∈ ω.getLast? := by simp [hgl]
    have hlast : ∀ j ∈ ω.getLast?, j = a := by
      intro j hj
      rw [hgl, Option.mem_some_iff] at hj
      exact hj.symm
    rcases hmem a (List.mem_of_mem_getLast? hamem) with rfl | rfl
    · exact Or.inr (eq_alternatingWord_of_forall_mem_pair (fun j hj => (hmem j hj).symm) hchain
        hlast)
    · exact Or.inl (eq_alternatingWord_of_forall_mem_pair hmem hchain hlast)

section

variable {cs}

/-- **A reduced word has no two adjacent equal letters.** Deleting such a pair leaves the product
unchanged and the word shorter, so the original word was not of minimal length. -/
theorem IsReduced.isChain_ne {ω : List B} (hω : cs.IsReduced ω) : ω.IsChain (· ≠ ·) := by
  revert hω
  induction ω with
  | nil => intro _; simp
  | cons a ρ ih =>
      cases ρ with
      | nil => intro _; simp
      | cons b τ =>
          intro hω
          have hρ : cs.IsReduced (b :: τ) := by simpa using hω.drop 1
          refine List.isChain_cons_cons.mpr ⟨?_, ih hρ⟩
          rintro rfl
          have hprod : π (a :: a :: τ) = π τ := by
            rw [cs.wordProd_cons, cs.wordProd_cons, cs.simple_mul_simple_cancel_left]
          have hle := cs.length_wordProd_le τ
          have heq := hω.eq
          rw [hprod] at heq
          simp only [List.length_cons] at heq
          omega

end

/-! ### Elements of a rank-two standard parabolic subgroup -/

/-- A reduced word all of whose letters are `i` or `i'` is one of the two alternating words of its
length. -/
theorem eq_alternatingWord_or_of_isReduced {i i' : B} {ω : List B} (hω : cs.IsReduced ω)
    (hmem : ∀ j ∈ ω, j = i ∨ j = i') :
    ω = alternatingWord i i' ω.length ∨ ω = alternatingWord i' i ω.length :=
  eq_alternatingWord_or_of_forall_mem_pair hmem hω.isChain_ne

/-- **Every element of a rank-two standard parabolic subgroup is spelled by an alternating word of
its own length.** Being of length `ℓ w`, that word is reduced. -/
theorem wordProd_alternatingWord_eq_of_mem_parabolic_pair {i i' : B} {w : W}
    (hw : w ∈ cs.parabolic {i, i'}) :
    π (alternatingWord i i' (ℓ w)) = w ∨ π (alternatingWord i' i (ℓ w)) = w := by
  obtain ⟨ω, hred, hωJ, rfl⟩ := cs.exists_isReduced_wordProd_eq_of_mem_parabolic hw
  have hmem : ∀ j ∈ ω, j = i ∨ j = i' := fun j hj => by simpa using hωJ j hj
  rw [hred.eq]
  rcases cs.eq_alternatingWord_or_of_isReduced hred hmem with h | h
  · exact Or.inl (by rw [← h])
  · exact Or.inr (by rw [← h])

/-- **The two alternating words of length `m` have the same product exactly when the rotation
`s i * s i'` is killed by `m`.** This is the dihedral arithmetic of a rank-two parabolic subgroup,
and the only computation in this file. -/
theorem wordProd_alternatingWord_eq_comm_iff (i i' : B) (m : ℕ) :
    π (alternatingWord i i' m) = π (alternatingWord i' i m) ↔ (s i * s i') ^ m = 1 := by
  have hinv : s i' * s i = (s i * s i')⁻¹ := by
    rw [mul_inv_rev, cs.inv_simple, cs.inv_simple]
  rw [cs.prod_alternatingWord_eq_mul_pow, cs.prod_alternatingWord_eq_mul_pow, hinv, inv_pow]
  rcases Nat.even_or_odd m with hm | hm
  · obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := hm
    have hev : Even m := ⟨p, hp⟩
    have hdiv : m / 2 = p := by omega
    simp only [ite_eq_left hev, one_mul, hdiv]
    rw [eq_inv_iff_mul_eq_one, ← pow_add, show p + p = m from hp.symm]
  · obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := hm
    have hnot : ¬Even m := by rw [hp]; simp [parity_simps]
    have hdiv : m / 2 = p := by omega
    simp only [ite_eq_right hnot, hdiv]
    rw [← inv_mul_eq_iff_eq_mul, cs.inv_simple, ← mul_assoc, ← pow_succ',
      eq_inv_iff_mul_eq_one, ← pow_add, show p + 1 + p = m from by omega]

/-- **The products of the alternating words repeat with period twice the order of the rotation
`s i * s i'`.** Only `(s i * s i') ^ n = 1` is used, so the period may be read off any exponent
killing the rotation. -/
theorem wordProd_alternatingWord_add_two_mul (i i' : B) {n : ℕ} (hn : (s i * s i') ^ n = 1)
    (m : ℕ) : π (alternatingWord i i' (m + 2 * n)) = π (alternatingWord i i' m) := by
  have hpar : Even (m + 2 * n) ↔ Even m := by
    simp only [Nat.even_iff]
    omega
  rw [cs.prod_alternatingWord_eq_mul_pow, cs.prod_alternatingWord_eq_mul_pow,
    show (m + 2 * n) / 2 = m / 2 + n from by omega, pow_add, hn, mul_one]
  simp only [hpar]

/-! ### Two left descents -/

/-- A left descent of `w` turns a reduced word for `s i * w` into a reduced word for `w`. -/
theorem isReduced_cons_of_isLeftDescent {i : B} {w : W} (hd : cs.IsLeftDescent w i) {ω : List B}
    (hω : cs.IsReduced ω) (hprod : π ω = s i * w) : cs.IsReduced (i :: ω) := by
  have hw : π (i :: ω) = w := by
    rw [cs.wordProd_cons, hprod, cs.simple_mul_simple_cancel_left]
  have hlen : ℓ (s i * w) + 1 = ℓ w := cs.isLeftDescent_iff.mp hd
  rw [IsReduced, hw, List.length_cons, ← hω.eq, hprod, hlen]

/-- **An element of a rank-two standard parabolic subgroup with two distinct left descents is
spelled by both alternating words of its length.** The two descents produce two reduced words with
different first letters, and the two alternating words of that length are the only candidates. -/
theorem wordProd_alternatingWord_eq_of_isLeftDescent_pair {i i' : B} (hne : i ≠ i') {w : W}
    (hw : w ∈ cs.parabolic {i, i'}) (hd : cs.IsLeftDescent w i) (hd' : cs.IsLeftDescent w i') :
    π (alternatingWord i i' (ℓ w)) = w ∧ π (alternatingWord i' i (ℓ w)) = w := by
  -- a reduced word for `w` beginning with a given left descent, with letters in `{i, i'}`
  have key : ∀ j : B, j ∈ ({i, i'} : Set B) → cs.IsLeftDescent w j →
      ∃ ω : List B, cs.IsReduced ω ∧ (∀ a ∈ ω, a = i ∨ a = i') ∧ π ω = w ∧
        ω.length = ℓ w ∧ ω.head? = some j := by
    intro j hj hdj
    have hmem : s j * w ∈ cs.parabolic {i, i'} :=
      mul_mem (cs.simple_mem_parabolic_of_isLeftDescent hw hdj) hw
    obtain ⟨ω, hred, hωJ, hprod⟩ := cs.exists_isReduced_wordProd_eq_of_mem_parabolic hmem
    have hredj : cs.IsReduced (j :: ω) := cs.isReduced_cons_of_isLeftDescent hdj hred hprod
    have hwprod : π (j :: ω) = w := by
      rw [cs.wordProd_cons, hprod, cs.simple_mul_simple_cancel_left]
    refine ⟨j :: ω, hredj, ?_, hwprod, ?_, rfl⟩
    · intro a ha
      rcases List.mem_cons.mp ha with rfl | ha
      · simpa using hj
      · simpa using hωJ a ha
    · rw [← hwprod, hredj.eq]
  obtain ⟨ω, hredω, hmemω, hprodω, hlenω, hheadω⟩ := key i (by simp) hd
  obtain ⟨ω', hredω', hmemω', hprodω', hlenω', hheadω'⟩ := key i' (by simp) hd'
  have hωne : ω ≠ ω' := fun h => hne (by rw [← Option.some_inj, ← hheadω, h, hheadω'])
  have hA := cs.eq_alternatingWord_or_of_isReduced hredω hmemω
  have hB := cs.eq_alternatingWord_or_of_isReduced hredω' hmemω'
  rw [hlenω] at hA
  rw [hlenω'] at hB
  rcases hA with hA | hA <;> rcases hB with hB | hB
  · exact absurd (hA.trans hB.symm) hωne
  · exact ⟨hA ▸ hprodω, hB ▸ hprodω'⟩
  · exact ⟨hB ▸ hprodω', hA ▸ hprodω⟩
  · exact absurd (hA.trans hB.symm) hωne

/-- The rotation `s i * s i'` is killed by the length of an element of `cs.parabolic {i, i'}` with
two distinct left descents. -/
theorem pow_length_eq_one_of_isLeftDescent_pair {i i' : B} (hne : i ≠ i') {w : W}
    (hw : w ∈ cs.parabolic {i, i'}) (hd : cs.IsLeftDescent w i) (hd' : cs.IsLeftDescent w i') :
    (s i * s i') ^ (ℓ w) = 1 := by
  obtain ⟨h, h'⟩ := cs.wordProd_alternatingWord_eq_of_isLeftDescent_pair hne hw hd hd'
  exact (cs.wordProd_alternatingWord_eq_comm_iff i i' (ℓ w)).mp (by rw [h, h'])

/-- **An element of `cs.parabolic {i, i'}` with two distinct left descents has length exactly the
order of the rotation `s i * s i'`.** The order divides the length by
`CoxeterSystem.pow_length_eq_one_of_isLeftDescent_pair`; were the length at least twice the order,
the periodicity of the alternating words would spell `w` by a strictly shorter word. -/
theorem length_eq_orderOf_of_isLeftDescent_pair {i i' : B} (hne : i ≠ i') {w : W}
    (hw : w ∈ cs.parabolic {i, i'}) (hd : cs.IsLeftDescent w i) (hd' : cs.IsLeftDescent w i') :
    ℓ w = orderOf (s i * s i') := by
  have hpos : 0 < ℓ w := by
    have := cs.isLeftDescent_iff.mp hd
    omega
  have hdvd : orderOf (s i * s i') ∣ ℓ w :=
    orderOf_dvd_of_pow_eq_one (cs.pow_length_eq_one_of_isLeftDescent_pair hne hw hd hd')
  have hne0 : orderOf (s i * s i') ≠ 0 := by
    rintro h0
    rw [h0, zero_dvd_iff] at hdvd
    omega
  refine Nat.eq_of_dvd_of_lt_two_mul (by omega) hdvd ?_
  rcases Nat.lt_or_ge (ℓ w) (2 * orderOf (s i * s i')) with hlt | hge
  · exact hlt
  -- a length at least twice the order would leave a strictly shorter word spelling `w`
  have hA := (cs.wordProd_alternatingWord_eq_of_isLeftDescent_pair hne hw hd hd').1
  have hper := cs.wordProd_alternatingWord_add_two_mul i i' (pow_orderOf_eq_one (s i * s i'))
    (ℓ w - 2 * orderOf (s i * s i'))
  rw [show ℓ w - 2 * orderOf (s i * s i') + 2 * orderOf (s i * s i') = ℓ w from by omega] at hper
  have hle := cs.length_wordProd_le (alternatingWord i i' (ℓ w - 2 * orderOf (s i * s i')))
  rw [hper.symm.trans hA, length_alternatingWord] at hle
  omega

/-- An element of `cs.parabolic {i, i'}` with two distinct left descents is no longer than the
Coxeter-matrix entry `M i i'`: its length is the order of `s i * s i'`, which divides `M i i'`. -/
theorem length_le_of_isLeftDescent_pair {i i' : B} (hne : i ≠ i') (hM : M i i' ≠ 0) {w : W}
    (hw : w ∈ cs.parabolic {i, i'}) (hd : cs.IsLeftDescent w i) (hd' : cs.IsLeftDescent w i') :
    ℓ w ≤ M i i' := by
  rw [cs.length_eq_orderOf_of_isLeftDescent_pair hne hw hd hd']
  exact Nat.le_of_dvd (Nat.pos_of_ne_zero hM)
    (orderOf_dvd_of_pow_eq_one (cs.simple_mul_simple_pow i i'))

/-- **The rank-two parabolic factor of an element with two distinct left descents inherits both
descents.** The factorization is the one of `CoxeterSystem.existsUnique_mem_parabolic_mul`, whose
lengths add. -/
theorem exists_mem_parabolic_pair_mul_of_isLeftDescent_pair {i i' : B} {w : W}
    (hd : cs.IsLeftDescent w i) (hd' : cs.IsLeftDescent w i') :
    ∃ x v : W, x ∈ cs.parabolic {i, i'} ∧ cs.IsLeftDescent x i ∧ cs.IsLeftDescent x i' ∧
      w = x * v ∧ ℓ w = ℓ x + ℓ v := by
  obtain ⟨⟨x, v⟩, ⟨hx, hv, rfl⟩, -⟩ := cs.existsUnique_mem_parabolic_mul {i, i'} w
  have hadd : ∀ y ∈ cs.parabolic ({i, i'} : Set B), ℓ (y * v) = ℓ y + ℓ v := fun y hy =>
    cs.length_mul_of_forall_not_isLeftDescent hy hv
  have hdesc : ∀ j : B, j ∈ ({i, i'} : Set B) → cs.IsLeftDescent (x * v) j →
      cs.IsLeftDescent x j := by
    intro j hj hdj
    have hsx : s j * x ∈ cs.parabolic ({i, i'} : Set B) :=
      mul_mem (cs.simple_mem_parabolic hj) hx
    have h₁ : ℓ (s j * (x * v)) = ℓ (s j * x) + ℓ v := by
      rw [← mul_assoc]; exact hadd _ hsx
    rw [IsLeftDescent, h₁, hadd x hx] at hdj
    rw [IsLeftDescent]
    omega
  exact ⟨x, v, hx, hdesc i (by simp) hd, hdesc i' (by simp) hd', rfl, hadd x hx⟩

/-- **Tits' lemma.** If `i ≠ i'` are both left descents of `w`, then `w` splits as a rank-two
parabolic factor times a remainder, the lengths adding, and the parabolic factor is spelled by
*both* alternating words of length `orderOf (s i * s i')`.

Classically the exponent is the Coxeter-matrix entry `M i i'`; the order of `s i * s i'` divides it
(`CoxeterSystem.simple_mul_simple_pow`), and the two are equal by Tits' theorem on the geometric
representation, which is unavailable here — see the module docstring. The bound this yields is
`CoxeterSystem.length_le_of_isLeftDescent_pair`. -/
theorem exists_wordProd_alternatingWord_mul_of_isLeftDescent_pair {i i' : B} (hne : i ≠ i')
    {w : W} (hd : cs.IsLeftDescent w i) (hd' : cs.IsLeftDescent w i') :
    ∃ v : W, 0 < orderOf (s i * s i') ∧
      w = π (alternatingWord i i' (orderOf (s i * s i'))) * v ∧
      w = π (alternatingWord i' i (orderOf (s i * s i'))) * v ∧
      ℓ w = orderOf (s i * s i') + ℓ v := by
  obtain ⟨x, v, hx, hdx, hdx', rfl, hlen⟩ :=
    cs.exists_mem_parabolic_pair_mul_of_isLeftDescent_pair hd hd'
  obtain ⟨h, h'⟩ := cs.wordProd_alternatingWord_eq_of_isLeftDescent_pair hne hx hdx hdx'
  have hpos : 0 < ℓ x := by
    have := cs.isLeftDescent_iff.mp hdx
    omega
  rw [cs.length_eq_orderOf_of_isLeftDescent_pair hne hx hdx hdx'] at h h' hpos hlen
  exact ⟨v, hpos, by rw [h], by rw [h'], hlen⟩

end CoxeterSystem
